text:
Add one canonical **Reduced Source** primitive.

A reduced source is:

```text
ReducedSource {
  owner_id,
  source_interest,
  reducer_id,
  output_targets,
  scope,
  lifecycle,
}
```

The kernel owns:

1. registering the source interest;
2. serving source rows from cache/store;
3. marking the source dirty when relevant events/account state change;
4. running a deterministic reducer;
5. diffing previous vs. next reduced output;
6. closing removed targets;
7. opening changed/new targets through existing registries;
8. triggering subscription recompilation.
